  Code's worktree tool created that folder, and the finish-branch skill leaves folders like that in place rather than
  deleting them itself. The branch can't be deleted while that worktree has it checked out.

  Everything in them is already on [38;5;153mmain[39m, so they're safe to remove. If you want them gone, say so, or run:
  [38;5;153m! git worktree remove --force .claude/worktrees/ratelimit && git branch -d worktree-ratelimit[39m
  [38;5;153m--force[39m is needed only because of leftover [38;5;153m__pycache__[39m folders, which Python regenerates. Because [38;5;153m.claude/[39m isn't in a
  [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, [38;5;153mgit status[39m on [38;5;153mmain[39m lists it as untracked until the worktree is removed.

